# Lifecycle Transition Writer Contract

- Each covered sign-in, sign-up, sign-out and session-limit carrier has one migration-owned state
  reference and one named transition surface. The transition table is the only legal-edge source.
- Lock and reload the owner, use the owning database clock, recheck expiry and source state, and
  write auxiliary facts in the same transaction. Caller-supplied `allowed_from`, `now`, state or
  terminal fields are not transition authority.
- Terminal states are absorbing. Refuse stale, illegal, conflicting, already-terminal and
  unexpected transitions; do not write `FAILED` as a generic escape hatch or turn a refusal into a
  guessed terminal outcome.
- Do not write lifecycle `status_id`, `state_id`, `state` or `step` directly from controllers,
  jobs, operations or callbacks. Initial row construction is distinct from a later transition.
- When a state or status axis changes, update its canonical Mermaid diagram and the matching section
  of `docs/mermaid/idp-state-machine-transition-inventory.md` in the same change.
